<title>INDIA: Indian soybeans stay slow and weak.</title>
<headline>Indian soybeans stay slow and weak.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices fell a further 100-150 rupees per tonne on Tuesday as 1,200 tonnes arrived at markets where business was thin.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were steady in thin trading.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were down, reflecting international markets. Soymeal was down by $8-9 and rapeseed extraction was down by $6-7 per tonne today. Soymeal yellow was $302-304 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was $107-108 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports in export and was 3,800-3,825 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on rail) condition. Business volume was dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
